# Build output lives in build/<preset> (see CMakePresets.json).
build/
cmake-build-*/
out/
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Generated by the firmware embedding step
**/fwEmbeddedFirmware.cpp
**/fwEmbeddedFirmware.h

# Runtime catalog: UF2 payloads are not source
catalog/*.uf2

# probe/ holds the CPU-prober image only. Its SOURCE is not here: the prober is
# wiliOGBsp's apps/cpuprobe, built there so it inherits the FreeWili OG board
# header (16 MB flash, PICO_FLASH_SPI_CLKDIV 4, clk_peri following clk_sys).
# The previous prober was built here for PICO_BOARD=pico and did not boot.
# These patterns are belt-and-braces so a stray in-tree build can never be
# committed.
#
# probe.uf2 is the ONE exception, and it is committed deliberately. Two hard
# requirements collide: the app must be a single self-contained executable (so
# the prober has to be embedded in it), and building the DESKTOP app must not
# require an ARM cross-toolchain or a firmware checkout (so it cannot be built
# from source during that build). 49 kB in git is the price of both.
#
# The objection to committing it -- a binary drifting out of sync with the
# source it claims to come from, on the CPU with no recovery path -- is real,
# and is answered rather than ignored: cmake/ProbeProvenance.cmake hashes
# probe.uf2 at configure time against the constant recorded in
# src/flash/fwCpuProbe.h and FAILS THE BUILD on a mismatch, additionally hashing
# apps/cpuprobe's main.c and CMakeLists.txt whenever a wiliOGBsp checkout is
# reachable; and identifyCpus() re-checks the image's hash at run time before
# writing it to a board. Drift is loud, not silent. See probe/README.md.
probe/*.uf2
!probe/probe.uf2
probe/*.elf
probe/*.bin
probe/*.hex
probe/*.dis
probe/*.map

# Embedded firmware images: 20+ MB of binaries do not belong in git history.
# manifest.json and README.md (which document how to obtain them) are kept.
firmware/*.uf2
# Stale checksum scratch file from wherever the images were obtained; the
# embedder computes its own hashes from the actual bytes and does not read it.
firmware/checksums.txt

# Loose UF2 images dropped in the repo root while testing a flash. The only
# committed UF2 in this tree is probe/probe.uf2 (see above); anything at the
# top level is a scratch copy of somebody's firmware build.
/*.uf2

# The generated remote catalog: tools/build_catalog.py copies whole .uf2
# images in here so the tree can be uploaded to docs.freewili.com as-is, and
# those are the same multi-megabyte binaries that are kept out of git
# everywhere else. publish/sources.json and publish/README.md -- the authored
# input and the upload procedure -- are committed; the build product is not.
publish/out/

# Packaged release archives. The published build is a GitHub Release asset,
# not a file in git history -- see the download link in README.md.
release/

# AI assistant working files: session scratch, generated plans, task logs and
# per-tool config. None of it is source, all of it is full of local absolute
# paths, and it is regenerated on demand.
.superpowers/
docs/superpowers/
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.aider*
.windsurfrules
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md

# Editors / OS
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.user
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
